    "message": {
     "content": "**Yes, you should accept this offer.** \n\nGetting a **$200,000 cash sign-on bonus** alongside a base match ($240,000) and $1.08M in RSUs without holding a competing written offer is an outstanding outcome. For an L6 PM at Google, a $200k sign-on is near the absolute top of their discretionary band.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Updated Financial Picture\n\nBecause Google uses a front-loaded vesting schedule (**33% / 33% / 22% / 12%**), your compensation for the first two years is extraordinary:\n\n| Component | Meta (Current) | Google Year 1 | Google Year 2 |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Base Salary** | $240,000 | $240,000 | $240,000 |\n| **Target Bonus** | $36,000 (15%) | $48,000 (20%) | $48,000 (20%) |\n| **RSU Vesting** | ~$200,000 | **$356,400** (33%) | **$356,400** (33%) |\n| **Sign-On Bonus** | \u2014 | **$200,000** | \u2014 |\n| **Total Comp (TC)** | **~$476,000 \u2013 $526,000** | **$844,400** | **$644,400** *(+ Y1 Refresher)* |\n\n#### Key Takeaways:\n* **Year 1:** You are netting **~$844,400**, representing an immediate **+$318,000 to +$368,000 premium** over your current Meta compensation.\n* **Two-Year Cumulative Upside:** Over your first 24 months, you will earn roughly **~$1.49M at Google** vs. **~$1.05M at Meta**\u2014a net gain of over **$440,000**.\n* **Cash vs. Equity Risk:** By giving you the $200k as guaranteed liquid cash upfront instead of equity, Google removed market volatility risk for that chunk of compensation.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Why You Should Not Push Further\n\n* **They matched your exact dollar-for-dollar ask:** You told them you were walking away from $200,000 in unvested RSUs, and they gave you precisely that in cash sign-on plus matched your $240k base. \n* **Diminishing returns / relationship risk:** When a recruiter returns with a 6-figure sign-on and explicitly designates it as their \"best and final offer\" (BAFO), pushing a third time risks coming across as adversarial or transactional right before joining your future team.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Check These 3 Details Before Signing\n\nBefore you put pen to paper, clarify the following administrative details with your recruiter:\n\n1. **Sign-On Payment Schedule & Clawback:**\n   * Is the $200,000 paid as a lump sum in your first 1\u20132 paychecks, or split across Year 1 and Year 2 (e.g., $100k / $100k)?\n   * Verify the clawback clause (standard is a prorated repayment if you voluntarily leave within the first 12 months).\n2. **Start Date Optimization:**\n   * Align your start date so you don't leave Meta right before a quarterly vest or bonus payout that is already within reach (e.g., if you have a vest date in 3\u20134 weeks, set your Google start date after that vest settles).\n3. **Team & Scope Confirmation:**\n   * Ensure your written offer specifies the intended team, reporting line, and office location (SF vs. Mountain View/Sunnyvale) you agreed to.",
